From 822d404c57d0245a407f8bd15c524591f595ad97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:14:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Blu-ray chapter thumbnails

The chapter thumbnails of a Blu-ray (folder or ISO, menus or not) stayed
placeholders: they were asked for as image://video@.../index.bdmv?chapter=N,
and discs are not extracted from. The player now names the clip each chapter
starts in (libbluray chapter clip_ref) and its time in that clip, and the
bookmarks dialog asks for BDMV/STREAM/<clip>.m2ts at that time (new "time"
option of the video thumbnail loader, ExtractThumbToTexture with a time).

Seeking into such a clip for a thumbnail gave up after "streams x 160"
packets of any stream; a UHD clip carries a dozen streams and TrueHD alone
about 1200 packets a second, so most chapters ran out before the first
keyframe. Up to 400 video packets now count, within a large overall bound.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
